The "cx-tail (sol) events re-arm" stream has ended.

## Iteration 1 — Inspected and Revised

I reviewed `OUT/it1/close-000-pair.png`, `close-035-pair.png`, `close-090-pair.png`, `close-180-pair.png`, and `OUT/contact-sheet.png` (which also includes the rear 3/4 and overhead views).

**Observations:**
- The front and 35-degree views still show gray, broken patches beneath the coat.
- The side view has a rounder outline but reveals a broad, exposed gray core between isolated brown strips.
- The rear view looks like scattered leaf tips over gray clay, with dark holes and insufficient continuous fur coverage.
- The overhead view confirms that the cards do not yet cover the bulb. This is a visual defect, even though the geometric noise diagnostic has improved.

**Measured Evidence:**
- `OUT/it1/verification.json` (generated by `OUT/it1-build.log`):
  - Base mesh remains 35,789 vertices / 27,700 triangles; indices are identical.
  - Outside-region vertices (23,375/23,375) and triangles (20,289/20,289) are identical.
  - Original non-position/normal bufferViews, including plume and images, are byte-identical.
  - Added cards: 640 triangles.
  - Welded p90 Laplacian source: 7.246749692691838 mm → smoothed 1.062448152156988 mm. Note: This is source-to-result geometry only, not a likeness score or visual pass.

**Build Status:**
- The initial authoring run failed before GLB/render due to an integer frame-vector dtype (`OUT/it1-initial-error.log`). I corrected the JSON vector to float.
- The complete run succeeded (`OUT/it1-build.log`). No script changes were made after the successful build.

**Next Steps (Iteration 2):**
- Data-only change.
- Increase circumferential overlap.
- Reduce root burial and move mid/tip surfaces outward.
- Reverse the small cup so its center bows outward.
- Maintain the same smoothing/attachment protection and GLB preservation method.
- Retain all Iteration 1 artifacts.
